Original commit body from 5c2e595df11cf62b5037989c27645f876826a56a:

INV-pusin's ratified statement — a module named solely by an import or a TYPE
ANNOTATION performs no I/O and must not withhold a boundary verdict — held for
cpp's `using std::cout;` and failed for `using S = std::string;`, whose scoped
path sits under `type_descriptor`.

That context was NOT appended when the defect was filed, because in the cpp
grammar it also covers casts and template arguments and the filing recorded
that "whether every member of that population is genuinely a type annotation
... is NOT established". It is now, by parsing each form and calling the
production `_scoped_context_kind`: the context covers exactly type alias,
`static_cast<std::string>(y)` and `std::vector<std::string>`, and all three
NAME a type and read no value. Template arguments are by far the largest
member — rocksdb 2359 occurrences against 126 aliases — so the filed defect is
the smallest part of what this fixes.

A CLOSURE CAN SATISFY THE REPRO AND NOT THE STATEMENT, so twelve further forms
were enumerated. Two more leak:

  class A : public std::exception     base_class_clause   FIXED, added
  for (std::string x : v)             for_range_loop      DELIBERATELY NOT

`for_range_loop` covers BOTH halves of the loop — the variable's type and the
RANGE EXPRESSION — and `for (auto& l : std::cin)` puts `std::cin` in the same
context. Skipping it would suppress a genuine stream read, which is the
false-all-clear direction and the same hazard this item names for
`std::cout << 1`. Separating them needs FIELD-level granularity, which
`skip_context_kinds` does not have. The residual over-withholds, which is safe,
and a test pins the range expression as still emitting so the cost of "fixing"
it is visible to whoever tries.

`call_expression` is likewise untouched: it is where genuine calls live and
`std::ofstream("f")` is one.

Measured A/B over the five cpp repos carrying a survey baseline, both arms,
fresh cache each, arm-take proven by reading the tuple out of the shipped
module: 12,556 -> 8,566 module_attr_ref edges (-3,990, -31.8%), and 0 of 15
verdicts moved. rocksdb -2494 (-59%), powerdns -1219, shaka-packager -251,
libzmq -15, plasma-desktop -11. The zero verdict movement is the SAFETY result:
this removes withholding, so a verdict turning clean would be a claim about the
world needing per-repo defence, and none did. The two surviving inconclusives
are held by other rungs entirely (glsl has no catalogue; shaka-packager has an
opaque-launch disclosure).

Also: the test harness was asserting against tuples the analyzers no longer
ship. test_base.py carried hand-copies of both skip tuples, and RUST_SKIP still
listed `use_declaration`, which INV-pusin's SECOND closure had moved into
`skip_ancestor_kinds` because the grammar wraps every `use` form but the bare
one. So every rust test in that class passed through the mechanism production
had abandoned — the right answer for the wrong reason, blind to a regression in
the real path. A parity test now reads both tuples out of the shipped analyzers
and fails if either copy drifts, and the rust helper passes the ancestor kinds
so those tests exercise what actually runs.

